  "caption": "The chained S-eps probability retains a scale discrepancy despite component calibration. Its stored pooled diagnostic slope is 1.7617 and intercept is 0.9794. The four panels use the same 11,256 external OOF observations (128 V<=2 cases) and ten pre-specified equal-width probability bins. Points show the mean stored probability and empirical event frequency in each nonempty bin; counts are listed in bin order, with the final bin including 1. Intercepts, slopes and Brier scores are read from existing results; no calibration is refitted. Raw-versus-calibrated Top-20 overlap is 20/20 within every fold for B-eps, L-single and L-hash4, but 15/20, 16/20 and 16/20 after pooling, respectively. This comparison is not recorded for S-eps. Pooled diagnostics assess probability scale and do not replace the fold-specific screening endpoint; sparse high-probability bins remain descriptive.",
